  "discussion": "A moderate, medium-period north (010 degrees) swell will gradually decline through Wednesday. Expect north shore surf on all islands to slowly decline today and fade late Wednesday. A small north-northwest swell will be possible during the weekend, with a larger swell possible next Tuesday. Rough surf along east-facing shores will drop to seasonal average tonight as winds slightly taper and the north swell declines. A slight increase in east shore surf is expected Friday and Saturday. Mainly small background level surf will persist along south-facing shores during the next several days, with a small long-period swell possible on Friday.",
